{
  "slug": "sex-age-and-ancestry-differences-and-young-onset-pd",
  "concept": "Sex, age and ancestry differences and young-onset PD",
  "generated": "2026-11-28",
  "summary": "Source-anchored research for Sex, age and ancestry differences and young-onset PD. Run status: COMPLETED.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Measurements and reference values",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The ethnic-variation narrative review states that LRRK2 p.G2019S is the most common genetic cause of PD worldwide, accounting for 1% of sporadic PD and 4% of familial PD. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.3233/JPD-191763",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:19831f930580ec03e50f42a49495a6ce9647dd9a29c1c46e033da51f0a48668f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:650867401832c824d6336f8ae360f320b65491d84e1afd69b58ff8daa581e2a9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The same review reports LRRK2 p.G2019S prevalence of 30–39% in North African Berbers with PD and 26% in Ashkenazi Jewish PD cases, yet states that it seems to be completely absent in Nigerian PD patients. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.3233/JPD-191763",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3f5ef270d18e6fedd536c2a95f291b9465c8ab0d37c7e1b3643c8c9c3c04a145",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:46085b9ee3c2fcfea8e98eec5ed138cad383a28317a414210f2053799878c551"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The epidemiology review reports that increasing age is associated with increased Parkinson’s disease risk, consistent with the Parkinson’s Foundation description of incidence increasing with age. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11123577/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:6afd5db6c3191089e97f5eef62fa86a8ee6e83d55a53561e0773e40a6e2af4fe",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:35dbe89d047bbad0d12104236aa3b27fc357620c2e1789cef4831d52c93b0188",
            "ev:6cbb6f38aa174e31fd258894a676fed92604cbbaec16e3609fcf5c63668f8251",
            "ev:f508af222086b4525956d03ea152c744cd0d48c15b3c7bf1b15dc54b706916f9"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.parkinson.org/understanding-parkinsons/statistics"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the US Medicare study, age-standardized Parkinson disease incidence and prevalence were greater in men than women across the racial groups studied; the Parkinson’s Foundation also reports higher incidence estimates in men. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2865395/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7da1e626272ba53a585e72f10094f26f005143458acfba3ab96a0bb74d6091f1",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1a8a57cb0d17b2c34135391c3d24503571644a92d9fdd188d4241cb870e737c5",
            "ev:b9c10ada666d8d9dd5327355628a7f06035086ff7d14f25f2857ecde6e547558"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.parkinson.org/understanding-parkinsons/statistics"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society task force defines early-onset Parkinson’s disease as onset after 21 years but before 50 years. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9547138/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ade83478958b53e165c1509375813889a97a88a4bc75670cef2ab018098d8fff",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:26ef756138c84cd5e2a9f36a2d22cfbf3a86f3e3ee00890a2bccddcd742290cc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The task-force review reports that genetic predisposition may be more likely with younger age at Parkinson’s disease onset. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9547138/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:1f5c1b32dccbcdd235da8165b37172bcbf994b0ac3e8b24bd5f14213f7b56637",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:11c548797fd6f38f64f38f96e9edc77404ab080eb0a41f4ee126bb3965ac405b"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The task-force review reports that most studies find slower motor-symptom progression in early-onset than late-onset Parkinson’s disease. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9547138/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b20244123e707ab0c8f2f647b74bca690ff73c62051892174b869eaad7ab5752",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:09bd2d4bda97f33a3ead9a87390507c102c0322b41d27c44aa5e3811269fb30c"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The task-force review describes unemployment in early-onset Parkinson’s disease as a burden that can include social isolation and loss of purpose and self-esteem. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9547138/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7e22fbf6211e05d6a62d8d153fa7fb52dffd1db9b98b0407df7839630cf6653c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:9ece6a566adf8b15a290da8dce2194c573f7f0dd99e821c12a116e3138cff9fc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The US Medicare study reports lower mean age-standardized Parkinson disease prevalence among Black and Asian beneficiaries than among White beneficiaries in its historical study population. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2865395/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c69b9a89d9d6905a18edbb253ffe7a73ceafbb6b0df37c55a1bdcf738d908e32",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:8b48dabbdd4fcf19c6b4942e3ce5353083e0907b37188d2372323286f50192c1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The epidemiology review cautions that apparent ethnic differences in Parkinson’s disease risk may reflect differential access to health care. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11123577/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7fbcd003d5eaddba07a236c73add55b4f8a9b608a480880954b523472ee5e2cf",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:893fa7b34525346f3401132371e9d5329367ade3eda7bc85bf018e4d02672298"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the Korean genome-wide association study, the authors report the strongest Parkinson’s disease associations at the SNCA and PARK16 loci. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41531-023-00580-3",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:405b38cc302340daf4683969d0d00329b9f6adb871f0772875537a771aab5dd5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0fe6b4f0b2a6e2f4e106ac58036a76c02f158643e1da5d091bba4b9a9a4ca25d"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Korean study’s authors identify limited statistical power, particularly after sex stratification, as a limitation of their genetic association results. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41531-023-00580-3",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0865bddb271e2a28e922e825ce9194d32329152b3c619d8de7dd2ae260e4ce0f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:b24cac1e98f72c2ea51d11bbebb70d7770984f029d72634b72692b0f32857d56"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The FENS release states that a limitation of the presented study is the small number of samples investigated. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-07-08)",
          "source": "https://www.fens.org/news-activities/news/why-does-parkinsons-disease-affect-more-men-than-women-study-reveals-differences-in-gene-activity-in-the-brain",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c016c5cf9f2f797c5194dd78dfe466aa256dee64f296c83516ee60adb2da8ff9",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0f6a10ccce7d25a354d074185da3b49cbcfa026ec96d3bf267d066a863c2a071",
            "ev:73685f41fb9607d745742c3074e6bc16e0b8d6d66f8412e2515af600f5e7b658"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Sources differ on the sex gradient in Asian populations: the US Medicare study reports greater age-standardized prevalence and incidence in men than in women for all races studied, whereas Park and colleagues state that Parkinson's disease is more prevalent in women in Asian populations, including the Korean population. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2865395/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f78503364f5fb0181399b6aa50fc2450812d8fefedbb402e87c5d88dd64ae1cc",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:356a293207388a3de49d8f2f283a1102d916e1fec5313bd4995e4bc3f934c385",
            "ev:54e99f9f6505ae6aeb1d19c2c3c06cfd2d6c3cdc18f01516fc4efd20fa4eead4",
            "ev:62b5e52b34b341f765c19a22615d5534beedea4758b08b6a8db053a73d456373"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41531-023-00580-3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The review states that the GBA variants 84insGG and R496H increase risk of PD exclusively in Ashkenazi Jewish populations. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.3233/JPD-191763",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:5d8e6ddb326f5307ca58549c9cb98d8a6163127d57c1b03560f4e3723742b59b",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:d37266f6e336cdc625a830f13085f1c748169b006c7a5a1958d28b5f40c0c119"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society task force review states that the most frequent genetic mutations associated with EOPD are located on parkin (PARK2), PINK1 (PARK 6), the PARK7 gene, ATP13A2 (PARK9) and PLA2G6 (PARK14). (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9547138/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:318a439ed52eb53debbe5fcb159b0b52bc66642327b6a0f1e80054981f0ba53e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:9a94bb316681757e53792a5c6a4875eb41dd4ba24ede67c6880eaa1257096263",
            "ev:d1a0d5c20c6a9081bb13d44d57a89fd9c744018ced9a5cc0003678c2599cd0ac"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The task force recommends the term early-onset Parkinson’s disease rather than young-onset Parkinson’s disease. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9547138/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:4f75fd734065b248153009c6017f72d610cf156434d19a87d2c8eadaf66ddf72",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:6ae698ba4e7f3e37c500db75d6fc24a6389074c0ecbd0b424ecfc403b8d78b45"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The task-force review reports that levodopa-induced dyskinesia is more frequent with younger age at onset. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9547138/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:687f9eaf36bda26b392448a26cc3a259b6ba28c7fdf3463938f6f75367e67268",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:6c327e3492f2835fd7e5041ced2a1753f0f1fd0c1b00cb1ca53905fa2da61ae3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The epidemiology review cautions that self-declared race or ethnicity has been used as a surrogate for genetic ancestry despite reflecting sociocultural conditions more closely. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11123577/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a94ecc200b3668b20f4f827ef548ff2d0be249f88583d7b74df668648c02fe4d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:6b1db16e0f33b5d659108a9085a88a3ed081328701dac6608895e61f8e057089"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the Korean study’s male-only analysis, no single nucleotide polymorphism surpassed the genome-wide significance threshold after Bonferroni correction. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41531-023-00580-3",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:4c08b3f465ac1d7608bcd366422274dd233e62a7b0056318726c41b6b3b4ba4f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:e84dff3a4f98ca1f04540418eadd34852466569eb8cb7c9e6c8e33f581b7145f"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Schaffner and colleagues report more associations of blood DNAm with PD in females (69 regions) than in males (2 regions) in a region-based analysis of agricultural workers (71 early-stage PD cases, 147 controls). (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11076573/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:85f5150bea2fc7c59bd798927bc0734baf9d30463b195d2b37701428bd087b5c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:337dfb83a2b985df00a58355d160c37652a5edd5664da219698b5d010e59a7d6",
            "ev:e2dc3dab3776a58a977a2c2b92af68e4d716026eccb01d21863cf2f79c95ac11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A FENS press release states that research presented at the FENS Forum 2026 compared post-mortem brain samples from 73 people with PD (28 women and 45 men) with 24 controls (9 women and 15 men). (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-07-08)",
          "source": "https://www.fens.org/news-activities/news/why-does-parkinsons-disease-affect-more-men-than-women-study-reveals-differences-in-gene-activity-in-the-brain",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:24610212d89007cd108dff60e0919228f832a0c27d6dfc8beca10270894d366e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:07c6eb785b1b29e480d8b5354b8a02b52788d73a43ab66f6deecd758007c01ca",
            "ev:73685f41fb9607d745742c3074e6bc16e0b8d6d66f8412e2515af600f5e7b658",
            "ev:cead7d3b18023eedd843f232ecd7b76a99239b33949822b527a4e46d55639dc2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the FENS release, the presenting investigator reports that, across five brain regions, PD caused common changes regardless of sex, together with differences between men and women in gene activity in some cells and some brain regions. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-07-08)",
          "source": "https://www.fens.org/news-activities/news/why-does-parkinsons-disease-affect-more-men-than-women-study-reveals-differences-in-gene-activity-in-the-brain",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d1cd615017e54782f8d249ed1bffc64f4b925de3b476170e79b39b3a7e3ba6f5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:28d6e7b9e87e0711c660b4e2d6cc177d8a7ea6095ae23d4f4dba9b5fd5f4c9b6",
            "ev:73685f41fb9607d745742c3074e6bc16e0b8d6d66f8412e2515af600f5e7b658",
            "ev:abc931906612f8a6fc3fa9987ad82c307f67339d99336b90dd7dd4ef144207fc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The FENS release reports that mitochondria-linked gene activity differed between sexes in astrocytes and that myelin-related gene activity differed between sexes in oligodendrocytes. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-07-08)",
          "source": "https://www.fens.org/news-activities/news/why-does-parkinsons-disease-affect-more-men-than-women-study-reveals-differences-in-gene-activity-in-the-brain",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:549c855db7d5ab692be316d44ddebda4ba901b242fb66b6dea67d883f2fde91e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:73685f41fb9607d745742c3074e6bc16e0b8d6d66f8412e2515af600f5e7b658",
            "ev:e82f0bf4db4efc668e534360b41e0a2b48be6a5629d4aa43e41c2a7cd296ff9c"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
